kubeos-base (0.2.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Debian revision numbering: 0.1.0-1kubeos2 -> 0.2.0-1. The revision is a plain Debian one now
    instead of the 1kubeosN prefix the first uploads used; the upstream version is
    unchanged. The KubeOS distribution version lives in kubeos-base, which is 0.2.0.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0530

kubeos-base (0.1.0-1kubeos2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Depend on kubeos-kubernetes. Without it, "apt install kubeos-base" - the documented
    way to turn a Debian system into a KubeOS node - installed nine of the ten components
    and left kubelet/kubeadm/kubectl/kubernetes-cni unpinned, which is exactly what the
    pin exists to prevent. The ISO was unaffected because it lists kubeos-kubernetes
    itself, but the metapackage has to be complete on its own.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:55:00 +0530

kubeos-base (0.1.0-1kubeos1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: the metapackage that names this distribution version and pulls
    every KubeOS component, plus the archive keyring and sources line that let a node
    update itself with apt instead of needing a new ISO.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:20:00 +0530
